<title>UK: RTZ up on bullish coal output plans.</title>
<headline>RTZ up on bullish coal output plans.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Anglo-Australian mining group RTZ-CRA climbed on Friday morning after reports that the company plans to double its U.S. coal production capacity over the next 10 years.</p>
<p>RTZ shares, which fell heavily on Thursday amid fears about a strike at its Kennecott copper smelter in Utah, were up 4-1/2p at 983-1/2p with 175,000 shares traded by 0726 GMT.</p>
<p>On Thursday, Gregory Boyce, president of RTZ-CRA's Kennecott Energy division, said he expected low sulphur coal producers such as Kennecott to benefit from a tightening of the U.S. Clean Air Act in the year 2000.  </p>
<p>&quot;The coal outlook has helped matters and we feel the share shouldn't have dropped as far as it did on Thursday. That was overdone and there should be a bit more of a bounce,&quot; one market maker said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
